cellSaveData: a callback error returns CELL_SAVEDATA_ERROR_CBRESULT (CASPER-3)

USER report: the Pomeranian (every animal) locked in Survival. On first boot
TJ's "is there a save?" AutoLoad2 funcStat answers ERR_NODATA. savedata_execute
mapped that to CELL_SAVEDATA_ERROR_NODATA and both AutoLoad entries then turned
it into CELL_OK (an old flOw compat hack), so the game believed a save had
loaded, never built its first profile (0xBCC160, 0x37DE0 bytes), and later
autosaved the blank profile: every unlock flag 0. Hardware and RPCS3 return
CELL_SAVEDATA_ERROR_CBRESULT (0x8002B401) for any callback error
(build-oracle/20261014-173029/RPCS3.log); TJ's title FSM (func_001E683C)
compares against exactly that value to create the profile and autosave it.
c3-save1 (first boot, empty CWD): same call sequence as RPCS3, and the new
SYS-DATA is byte-identical to RPCS3's first-boot save (362 non-zero bytes).

